                <p class="text-center text-gray-600 mb-4 max-w-3xl mx-auto">Standard methods offer a static, lifelong snapshot of genetic risk. This research will pioneer a dynamic understanding by modeling how an exposure's causal impact changes over time, identifying critical windows of risk that were previously hidden.</p>
                 <button class="view-source-btn" data-title="Source: Aim 2" data-text="Background and Rationale: Understanding when and how exposures influence disease risk , such as CVD, throughout life and life stages is crucial. This knowledge will allow our group to understand how the genetics associations affect exposures dynamically across periods of life or lifetimes... Most research efforts focus on either machine learning or Mendelian Randomization (MR), but rarely integrate the two. Building upon the findings from the association analyses and AI modelling from Aim 1, our group aims to validate the causal underpinnings of omics signatures using time-varying MR techniques. This integrated strategy connects data-driven prediction with mechanistic understanding—moving our work from statistical association to actionable intervention.">Details</button>
